KVarN V2-runner compatibility fixes for vLLM 0.28.0.

These changes are applied after the 0.28 KVarN base port and the repo's DFlash2 patches. They keep sliding-window groups out of prefix-cache arithmetic, use the Mamba group's block size for resumed-state indexing, and harden DFlash2 selector buffers against degenerate scores.

Ported to 0.29.0: the four kv_cache_utils.py hunks are retired. Upstream rewrote that function as
resolve_kv_cache_block_sizes (#51718, #53896): the hash unit is now the GCD over prefix-cacheable groups
only and every spec's per-state alignment is checked, which is what the hunks did by hand for the
drafter's sliding-window groups. On this model the groups are the KVarN full-attention layers and the
Mamba layers at the aligned block (2176 tokens for k4v2_g128) and the drafter's sliding-window layers at
block 128 with their page padded to the primary page, so both trees compute the same scheduler block
(2176) and hash unit (128); the hunks changed nothing for this geometry, and the coordinator hunks below
still exempt a sliding-window block that does not divide the scheduler block.

